-- title:
--   Newform multiplicity two, or four, in a same-level Hecke corner
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field $k$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a two-dimensional $k$-space with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$). Let $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ be finite sets of naturals, all members of $S$ prime, with $p \in S_{\min}$, such that a prime $q \neq p$ lies in $S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some element of an inertia subgroup at a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $q$ acts non-trivially), and such that for $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N \geq 1$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, satisfy $p^2 \nmid N$, be divisible by every $q \in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$, be divisible by $q^2$ for every prime $q \neq p$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S_{\min}$, and be cube-free; assume the integral lattice in weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$ spans over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $N\,2\,S$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ in its non-units, and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Write $T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) $N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta$ for the localisation of $\mathbb T$ at $\theta$ with $\mathcal O$-coefficients. Let $M$ be a $T$-module and $\mathcal O$-module, compatibly (scalar tower), $B$ an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form on $M$, and assume $(M,B)$ is a corner realisation, in the sense of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.IsCornerRealization`](def/CuspForm_HeckeModuleCornerRealization.html#L19), of the pair $(p,\bar\rho)$ at level $N$ equal to the level $N$ of the anemic algebra: there are a commuting family of operators indexed by the generators at level $N$ away from $S$, a residual system $\bar\theta$ on those generators, an idempotent splitting of the resulting operator subalgebra with a chosen index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from that corner ring to $k$ sending each generator to $\bar\theta$ of it, an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ of $M$ with the corresponding corner submodule of $H^1(\Gamma_H(N),\mathcal O)$ (that submodule consisting of parabolic classes), under which $T_\ell$-multiplication on $M$ becomes the cohomological $T_\ell$ and $B$ becomes the pairing [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140), and with $\bar\theta(T_\ell) = \theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell \notin S$ not dividing $N$, $\bar\theta(U_q) = 0$ when $q^2 \mid N$, and $\bar\theta(U_p) \neq 0$ when $p \mid N$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two implications about the $\overline{\mathrm{Frac}(\mathcal O)}$-dimension of the simultaneous eigenspace, inside $M \otimes_{\mathcal O} \overline{\mathrm{Frac}(\mathcal O)}$, attached to an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : T \to \overline{\mathrm{Frac}(\mathcal O)}$, namely the intersection over all $t \in T$ of the $\chi(t)$-eigenspaces of the base change of multiplication by $t$: this dimension equals $2$ for every such $\chi$ if it is not the case that $p \mid N$ and $\bar\rho$ fails to be ordinary at $p$, and equals $4$ for every such $\chi$ if $p \mid N$ and $\bar\rho$ is not ordinary at $p$ (ordinarity at $p$ meaning that over each valuation subring above $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, on whose quotient inertia acts trivially).
--
--   This is the equal-level case of the multiplicity count for corner realisations of $H^1$: each $\overline{\mathrm{Frac}(\mathcal O)}$-point of the localised anemic Hecke algebra is the eigensystem of a newform of level dividing $N$, and the dimension of its eigenspace in the corner is computed prime by prime from the Atkin–Lehner–Li theory of oldforms together with the Eichler–Shimura description of $H^1$. It feeds the general (two-level) corner multiplicity statement [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_cube_dvd), and so the freeness and duality input of the modularity-lifting argument.
